# Attribution

This project implements the FASTR scanner-gradient artifact correction method
described by:

Rami K. Niazy, Christian F. Beckmann, Gian Domenico Iannetti, John M. Brady,
and Stephen M. Smith. “Removal of FMRI environment artifacts from EEG data
using optimal basis sets.” NeuroImage 28(3), 720–737 (2005).

The tracked implementation is written in Python and does not include the
upstream MATLAB source file. This project is not the FMRIB EEGLAB plug-in and
is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the FMRIB Centre or the
University of Oxford.

